   "date": "2018-11-28",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The bill removes the requirement for a six-year prison sentence before citizenship can be revoked for terrorism offences, requiring only a conviction, and replaces the dual-citizenship requirement with a condition that the person will not become stateless; it applies to convictions after 12 December 2005 and includes association with a terrorist organisation as a relevant offence."
